  "format": "top5",
  "allowLong": true,
  "allowLongReason": "three fixes plus the 'should you update' answer and where to find it; that answer is the value, and cutting to 48s drops it",
  "script": "Apple just shipped iOS twenty seven point oh point one, the first update to iOS 27. It fixes three bugs. Two only hit one iPhone. The third could hit yours.\n\nThe first two belong to the iPhone 18 Pro and Pro Max. When Face ID failed inside an app like Passwords, some of them froze and restarted. That was a software bug, so you don't need a new phone.\n\nThe second is in the camera: some 2x photos, shot at the widest aperture in certain light, came out with a color glitch. Apple says only a small number of phones had it.\n\nWhich leaves the one for everyone: pull down Notification Center and Control Center together, and your screen could stop responding to touch.\n\nShould you update? Apple lists no security fixes, so there's no rush. On an 18 Pro, though, do it today. Everyone else, whenever it suits you. It's in Settings, General, Software Update.\n\nKnow an 18 Pro owner? Send them this.",
